<title>ABU DHABI: UAE's GAMCO to announce maintenance contract.</title>
<headline>UAE's GAMCO to announce maintenance contract.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United Arab Emirates' Gulf Aircraft Maintenance Company (GAMCO) will on Tuesday announce it has won a contract to service British Royal Air Force aircraft, a company official said on Monday.</p>
<p>The five-year contract was awarded to GAMCO last week, the official, who requested anonymity, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He did not put a price tag on the deal or say when work on the aircraft would begin.</p>
<p>GAMCO is 60-percent owned by the Abu Dhabi government.</p>
</text>
